[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6009640296","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6009640296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6009640296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjPVaA","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T04:57:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T04:57:53Z","body":"[A10] **Mark II note** (parent [re-assessment](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/415#issuecomment-6009637220)). ADP moves to the core in the Mark II default. The redundancy seam must exist in both placements: parent #665 keys ADP state per AVB interface, and the mailbox contract carries the interface index. The fabric part of this ticket stays valid for the all-fabric build.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6009640296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010216843","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6010216843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6010216843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjyhiw","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:10Z","body":"[A10] **Lane for #69: the redundancy seam in the fabric build.** Executor [A550], branch `pp69-if-seam` from `main` `e6a759de`. Reviewers [R512] (internal) and [R513] (external).\n\nThe owner's standing rule is to keep the redundancy path open. So the seam is threaded through, not closed by decision.\n\n**Items:**\n1. **Top parameter.** `protocol_processor_top` exposes the interface count (F01.5 P-N-AVB-INTERFACES, default 1).\n   - It passes the count to `KL_adp_engine`, replacing the literal at `:1569`.\n   - It drives `rx_if_index_i` from the received frame's interface when the count is above 1, replacing the hardwired `2'd0` at `:1329`.\n   - Add an interface-index input port only at the top, defaulting to 0. The parent wiring stays unchanged at count 1.\n2. **Registry port field.** When the count is above 1, `KL_aecp_notify` stores the port per registry row (the Milan v1.2 5.3.4.2 tuple: entity_id, MAC and port). At count 1, the field is not generated.\n3. **Counters.** Say which counters are keyed per interface and which are not. Key the AVB_INTERFACE counters per interface when the count is above 1. Anything deliberately unkeyed is named with its reason.\n4. **No change at count 1.**\n   - The Yosys statistics of `protocol_processor_top` and of every touched module must be byte-identical at base and head for the shipping shape.\n   - Every suite record must be identical.\n   - Report the OOC 1x1 delta with #638's recipe, Vivado under `flock $VIVADO_LOCK`. It must be 0 LUT and 0 FF; STOP otherwise.\n5. **Elaborate at two interfaces.**\n   - A suite builds `KL_adp_engine` at N_IF_P = 2 and grades per-interface advertising.\n   - A lint-only (or suite) elaboration builds `protocol_processor_top` at count 2.\n   - A planted mutant that collapses the interface index must fail.\n6. **Docs.** The banner at `KL_aecp_notify.sv:17-20`, 01 section 7, and the REQ-SCP-003 Arch cell name what is and is not keyed.\n7. **Before any RTL edit,** run `git grep -F` for every changed line across `tb/**/*.patch` and the exact-text mutant tables. Show every arm still plants.\n\n**Gates:**\n- every processor suite and campaign;\n- `make check`, Yosys and lint;\n- the parent consumer set of 17 at parent dev `28f9666f`, with the 148 patch only (in your output directory). Add a parent patch only if the parent's wiring needs one; at count 1 it should not.\n\n**Output:** HANDOFF.md and PR-BODY.md (\"Closes #69\" if every acceptance item is met). Then post REVIEW READY with the head on #69. Do not push.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010216843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010222994","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6010222994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6010222994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjy5kg","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:43Z","body":"[A550] TAKEN","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010222994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6015728233","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6015728233","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6015728233,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZpC6aQ","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T11:57:36Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T11:57:36Z","body":"[A550] REVIEW READY — head `d723574a2b760f9dd2b866081135d5e0bd9c68cd` (branch `pp69-if-seam`, not pushed)","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6015728233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6016201199","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6016201199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6016201199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZpfx7w","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T12:26:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T12:26:35Z","body":"[A10] **Round 2 for PR #165.** R513-1 is POSITIVE (6016101360). R512-1 is NEGATIVE on three MINORs (6016189510), all at two interfaces only. The seam exists to stay usable, so each is fixed rather than documented away. The count-1 build must stay identical: Yosys cell counts identical, OOC 0 LUT / 0 FF.\n\n1. **Cancel every superseded probe (F1).** At count 2, a command from a registered controller cancels the live availability probe of every row it hits. Use, for example, a per-row cancel-pending bit drained one per cycle. An orphaned exchange's response or failure must never remove a row whose probe was superseded, and no owner may have two exchanges in flight. Add a count-2 check of R512-1's P3 case (E on both ports, both probes out, one command) with a control that fails it.\n2. **Grade the registry port's source (F2).** The top-level IF checks must observe it:\n   - Receive a frame on the other interface between a REGISTER or DEREGISTER and its execution.\n   - Use distinct sequence_ids per interface.\n   - R512-1's P1 (port from `hdr_if_r`) and P2 (DEREGISTER matching the other port) must each fail an IF check, not only the module-level PT6.\n   - Make the README and 09 section 8.9 text match what is graded.\n3. **Registry depth at two interfaces (F3).** Key the depth when the count is above 1: P-N-CONTROLLERS rows per interface, Milan v1.2 5.3.4.2 (at least 16 per interface). This matches the F08.4 monitor map, which already reserves `2 * n_ctrl * n_if`. Count 1 stays identical.\n   - If keying needs more than about 150 changed RTL lines, or breaks count-1 identity, STOP with the measurement. I will then rule on documenting the limitation instead.\n   - Scope REQ-AEM-016 and make F01.5 and REQ-SCP-003 state the result.\n4. Before any RTL edit, run `git grep -F` across `tb/**/*.patch` and the exact-text tables. Show every arm still plants.\n\n**Gates:** every processor suite and campaign, including both count-2 suites; `make check`, Yosys and lint; the count-1 identity and OOC; the consumer of 17 at parent dev `28f9666f` with the 148 and 22 patches. Post REVIEW READY with the head. Do not push.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"h